== conflicting operator rule
report-error .gitattributes rule ".devcontainer/* text eol=crlf" gives the DevContainer directory another line-ending treatment than the managed rule ".devcontainer/* text eol=lf", which adoption writes at the tail of the file, where it would override that rule; remove or change the rule, or list dev-container in adoption.decline, then rerun adopt
error .gitattributes rule ".devcontainer/* text eol=crlf" gives the DevContainer directory another line-ending treatment than the managed rule ".devcontainer/* text eol=lf", which adoption writes at the tail of the file, where it would override that rule; remove or change the rule, or list dev-container in adoption.decline, then rerun adopt
file .gitattributes ".devcontainer/* text eol=crlf\n\n# BEGIN praetor managed attributes (praetorctl adopt)\n# praetorctl audit hashes these files; keep their checkout bytes the same on every platform.\n.devcontainer/* text eol=lf\n# END praetor managed attributes\n"
== fresh adoption with docs:seo-portal
action create .gitattributes :: Created the managed attribute block that keeps the files audit compares byte for byte unconverted
file .gitattributes "# BEGIN praetor managed attributes (praetorctl adopt)\n# praetorctl audit hashes these files; keep their checkout bytes the same on every platform.\n.devcontainer/* text eol=lf\ntools/figures/** text eol=lf\ndocs/figures/*.ts text eol=lf\ndocs/assets/figures/* text eol=lf\ntools/figures/third_party/interfig/upstream/** -text\n# END praetor managed attributes\n"
